== Personality ==
[[File:S2E48 Lok 8.png|thumb|200px]]
Lok was just a normal, fun-loving high school student, struggling to stay awake in his classes and wishing for a life of adventure. After finding his father's [[Amulets]] and becoming a Seeker, Lok puts his enthusiasm, intuition and natural talent to the test as he is introduced to Sophie Casterwill, Dante Vale, and the world of Seekers in Huntik. {{source|A Seeker Is Born}} Lok eventually developed a close brotherly bond with Dante {{source|Memory Lane}}, whilst becoming best friends with [[Cherit]] with the latter always at Lok's side throughout their numerous escapades together. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} Being able to relate to being a novice in the Seeker world, Lok became a big brother to [[Den Fears]], supporting him and teaching him new spells. {{source|Boys Will Be Seekers}}

He is usually quite even tempered, but he can be remarkably aggressive when sufficiently angered. This is seen both when he gains perfect control over Lindorm, who bonds best when his Seeker is angry {{source|S1E12}}, and when he believed his father was dead at the hands of the Organization. {{source|S1E21}}

<!--- The following points, merged from 'Lok and Sophie,' need to be re-written ---
* In the Casterwill Client, when Sophie strikes a deal with Dante, she cares enough about Lok to include teaching him to be a seeker as well as finding out what happened to Eathon.
* In The Vampire Loses Its Fangs, while running away from titans, Lok grabs Sophie's hand several times to save her. While Sophie and Zhalia are fighting, Lok cries her name several times, indicating he's worried about her. When Zhalia is about to finish Sophie off, Lok throws himself between them, covering Sophie's body with his own, showing that he cares enough for Sophie to let himself be killed instead of her.
